  "summary": "Full assessment of all 774 English/Vietnamese passages — epigraph, dedication, Preface, Walton’s letters and the three volumes of the 1818 text — and both titles, by three separate-context assessors who each read every pair in one volume and checked consistency across the seven drafting parts. Victor’s studies, the creation, William and Justine, the glacier, the creature’s narrative, the destroyed mate, Clerval and Elizabeth’s deaths, the pursuit and the creature’s last speeches are complete, with the verse quotations kept as verse. The assessors scored the volumes 8.90, 8.85 and 8.85 with no major findings; the cross-part pronoun, terminology and naturalness issues they reported were revised. Fidelity, voice, imagery and mechanics are 9.0, naturalness 8.5. Unrounded weighted score 8.925 meets the unchanged 8.6 threshold. No unresolved major or critical issue remains.",
